# effect_declared_where_used — (repurposed from effect_unused_declaration). Shows
# the effect discipline positively: a PURE helper op declares NO effect (it only
# does arithmetic, README §8 "pure ops omit effects"), while main declares the
# write effect it actually uses. Both compile clean and the result is real.
#
# Correctness observation: pure scale(6) = 6*9 = 54, printed by the io op.
# Expected output: 54

EffectDeclaredWhereUsed is project
EffectDeclaredWhereUsed module examplesEffectDeclaredWhereUsed
EffectDeclaredWhereUsed target console
EffectDeclaredWhereUsed entry main

examplesEffectDeclaredWhereUsed is module
examplesEffectDeclaredWhereUsed path examples.effectDeclaredWhereUsed
examplesEffectDeclaredWhereUsed exports main
examplesEffectDeclaredWhereUsed purpose "Declare effects only where they are used"
examplesEffectDeclaredWhereUsed invariant "The pure helper carries no effect row"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32
ExitCode purpose "Process exit status"

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout
stdoutWriter purpose "Allow controlled writes to standard output"

scale is operation
scale in n Int64
scale out Int64
scale memory heap no
scale async no
scale purpose "Return n * 9 (pure: no effects)"
scale invariant "Performs no effects; pure arithmetic"
scale let nine immutable Int64 9
scale do mulCall
scale return scaled

mulCall is call
mulCall in scale
mulCall invokes math.multiplyInt64
mulCall arg left Int64 n
mulCall arg right Int64 nine
mulCall out scaled Int64

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap no
main async no
main purpose "Call the pure scale op and print its result under a write effect"
main invariant "Writes exactly one integer line: 54"
main let six immutable Int64 6
main let okCode immutable ExitCode 0
main let harnessName immutable String "effect_declared_where_used"
main let harnessExpected immutable Int64 54
main let noopDecoy immutable Int64 0
main let noopName immutable String "effect_declared_where_used: real result (not the no-op 0)"
main do computeCall
main do writeResult
main do noopCheck
main do harnessReport
main return harnessSummaryCode

computeCall is call
computeCall in main
computeCall invokes scale
computeCall arg n Int64 six
computeCall out total Int64

writeResult is call
writeResult in main
writeResult invokes test.assertEqualInt64
writeResult arg name String harnessName
writeResult arg expected Int64 harnessExpected
writeResult arg actual Int64 total


noopCheck is call
noopCheck in main
noopCheck invokes test.assertNotEqualInt64
noopCheck arg name String noopName
noopCheck arg expected Int64 noopDecoy
noopCheck arg actual Int64 total

harnessReport is call
harnessReport in main
harnessReport invokes test.summary
harnessReport out harnessSummaryCode ExitCode